a well-formed generated file, registered once, does not have (every Go program importing the package
starts; `google/protobuf/any.proto`, which it depends on, registered first, by Go's initialization order
of imports). The model does nothing: no translated code reads the registries,
`File_google_rpc_status_proto` or the package's descriptor tables (they are not translated: names-only or
skipped, `Code/google_golang_org/genproto/googleapis/rpc/status.toml`; only
`file_google_rpc_status_proto_init` reads them). Until 2026-11-25 the package was not translated (grpc's
`internal/status` was names only).

**The limitation (etcd-grove#57):** a conflicting registration (a descriptor of the same file path or full
name registered before, `reflect/protoregistry/registry.go:47-65`, `conflictPolicy = "panic"`) panics in
Go but not in the model; retired by the protobuf-go registry model (#37). -/
